<<<
to be regarded as undesirable Gallicisms, Gallio. Pl. -os, see -o(£)s 8. gallivant. See FACETIOUS FORMA- TIONS. gallop makes -oped, -oping; see -P-, -PP-, gallows, though originally a plural form, is now singular (set up a g. &c.); the plural is usually avoided, but when unavoidable is gallowses. galop, the dance, is so spelt; used
===
to be regarded as undesirable Gallicisms.

**Gallio.** Pl. *-os*, see ^^-O(E)S^^ 8.

**gallivant.** See ^^FACETIOUS FORMATIONS^^.

**gallop** makes *-oped, -oping*; see ^^-P-^^, ^^-PP-^^.

**gallows,** though originally a plural form, is now singular (*set up a g.* &c.); the plural is usually avoided, but when unavoidable is *gallowses*.

**galop,** the dance, is so spelt; used
>>>

